I'm sorry to say, but given that you've lost a large part of the data, 
you're almost certainly hosed.  The recover tool won't be able to help.

If it's any consolation, it quite probably couldn't have helped anyway: 
it expects to build the level files into a save file, but I don't think 
it has any way to deal with a partially saved game (though I must admit 
I've never seen a scenario like this, so I'm not certain what it would do).

It's probably _possible_ to hand-hack a set of level files that could be 
merged into whatever you have left in the partial save file, but I've 
never heard of anyone managing that and it would certainly take longer 
than six hours to do.

For future reference, at least, it's important not to actually _move_ 
any of the files before running recover; you should make copies of any 
save files and any level files first, though, since recover will 
overwrite an old save file and delete the level files when it runs.

